{
  "_comment_accounts": "player_accounts is MIGRATED on the first boot of the auth code (argon2id hashes; admin=true -> site admin and group owner) and never used to log in again. Keep it until that deploy has been proven on a phone - it is the rollback's login - then delete it together with jwt_secret.",
  "db_url": "sqlite:///./app.db",
  "player_accounts": [
    { "name": "Roli", "password": "change-me-roli", "admin": true },
    { "name": "Flo", "password": "change-me-flo", "admin": false }
  ],
  "_comment_jwt": "jwt_secret only lets POST /auth/exchange trade a pre-cookie login token for one session; empty makes the exchange answer 410.",
  "jwt_secret": "dev-change-me",
  "push_vapid_public_key": "",
  "push_vapid_private_key_file": "./vapid_private_key.pem",
  "push_vapid_subject": "mailto:you@example.com",
  "push_ttl_seconds": 300,
  "log_level": "INFO",
  "_comment_smtp": "Optional - these five turn email on (verification links and recovery by email); empty means off. All five or none: a half-set refuses to boot. Production: smtp.privateemail.com, 465, smtp_user = the login mailbox, smtp_pass = its password (an application password if it has 2FA), smtp_from = no-reply@lorbeerkranz.xyz (an alias of that mailbox). Put them here only on the production server, and only after `manage.py mail-test` passed the Gmail check (inbox, SPF and DKIM PASS - AGENTS.md section 7), then `docker compose restart backend`. A development or test server refuses them; use MAIL_SINK_DIR=<dir> (env) there instead, which writes each mail to a file and delivers nothing.",
  "smtp_host": "",
  "smtp_port": 465,
  "smtp_user": "",
  "smtp_pass": "",
  "smtp_from": "",
  "_comment_auth": "No auth setting belongs in this file (the smtp_* keys above are mail, not auth). app_env, trusted_proxy_hops, auth_origin, auth_rp_id, auth_rp_name, auth_dev_origin, password_hash_profile and session_ttl_days are read from the environment (APP_ENV, TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS, ...) and defaulted in code: docker-compose.yml sets APP_ENV=production and TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1, the Makefile sets AUTH_DEV_ORIGIN=1 APP_ENV=development for dev. ws_require_auth is gone."
}
